This repository holds two different things, under two different sets of terms.
Read this page before the licence text below it.

1. THE PACKAGING — the scripts, the manifests, the workflows and the
   documentation written for this repository — is licensed under the MIT
   licence, reproduced below.

2. THE BUNDLES THEMSELVES — everything inside a release archive — are
   REDISTRIBUTIONS of the Kha SDK and its toolchain, and are NOT covered by the
   licence below. Each component keeps the licence its authors gave it. Those
   licences are listed, in full, in the THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md carried inside
   every archive and generated from the files actually present in it.

   Among them: Kha and Kore under the zlib licence, whose clause 3 says their
   notice may not be removed or altered from a distribution; the Haxe standard
   library under MIT; and THE HAXE COMPILER BINARY UNDER THE GNU GENERAL PUBLIC
   LICENSE VERSION 2, which obliges anyone redistributing it to supply the
   complete corresponding source for that exact version.

   That obligation is met by section 3(a) — accompaniment, not a promise. The
   Haxe source for the exact commit each bundle was built from is published as
   an asset on the same release, beside the bundle itself. Nobody has to ask for
   it and nobody has to keep an offer open.

Nothing below grants any right over the redistributed software in point 2.

